Z||000000||Formula 18||01-14-2001||02:08 AM||||Hey guys what do you think about this turbo on a stock 2.8 or a mild 3.1 (with all this talk about low compresion 3.2 a turbo seems like a schweet idea).... <A HREF="http://www.turboneticsinc.com/comp_maps/fig4.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.turboneticsinc.com/comp_maps/fig4.html</A> <BR>It is a T-3 with a 60 AR trim the exhaust has a ar of .63 It came from a T-bird turbo.<P>One more question. Does the compressor shaft spin on oil? The bearing seem tight but there is a slight bit of play from side to side. Is there supposed to be ANY play at all or does it ride on a little oil to keep it lubed? <BR>I have planed on a rebuild anyway but was hoping it could do W/O sience it was a pretty low mile car. <BR>If i do rebuild where is the best place to get a kit. <P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula<P>[This message has been edited by Formula 18 (edited 01-14-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by Formula 18 (edited 01-14-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by Formula 18 (edited 01-14-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Formula 18 (edited 01-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-14-2001||08:33 AM||||I have a 3.1 out of a Z-24 with a turbo. it has oil lines running to bearing. And it runs like a bat outta h__l.<P>mine would spin by just blowing air thru it<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 01-14-2001).]||||reg||1
