Z||000003||hugh||01-15-2001||07:10 AM||||Look at the RPM's of the turbos.They have to spin free.If you can feel any side play it is too much.They are engine oil lubricated so they do ride on a film of oil.Turbonetics is a good place to get a rebuilt cartridge.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||01-15-2001||11:01 AM||||you'll need about 27lbs per minute to support your motor at 65% and 121,000 rpm the tiny T3 will support it.. it'll ramp up quick and pull the 4500 and start to drop off.. the design one kit that Preditor has has a TINY T-28 it spools fast and makes a adaquite boost but the boost drops off after 4500.  it will run forever this way cause there is no major stresses on the motor in the upper RPM ranges...where turbos do their best work. ok it'll kick some serious @$$ in the 1/8th mile or stop light racing but try and stay off the highway the turbo will heat up and all the boost your making will wipe out the motor to heat soak and intake air temps being sky high. try and get a T-04e.  like this one..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newtoy2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/newtoy2.jpg</A>  or i'll seell ya this one for $600... retails for $680... it's a T04e (40)||||reg||1
